  "checkpoints": {
    "description": "The §8.1 checkpoint commitment, byte for byte. `state` is the part of the registry §8.1 requires committed — the name tree, the active prices, the pending set and, since r16, the unreserved set — and `logHash` is an input, the §8.2 log hash at this height. `nameRoot`, `pricesRoot`, `pendingRoot`, `unreservedRoot` and `commitment` are derived. Two implementations that agree on every other file here and disagree on this one publish checkpoints that never match. These values are r22, which removed the pending `U` (tag 0x09) when a `U` became effective on landing. **That removal moves no bytes**: the pending set concatenates its categories with no separators and no count, so a category with no entries contributed nothing even when it existed. Every case below whose state was reachable under r21 keeps its r21 value; the three that carried a pending `U` pinned a state that can no longer occur, and were re-authored or removed rather than refilled.",
